# KEYFLOW Frontend — Environment Variables Template
# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) in the frontend directory and fill in your actual values.
# NEVER commit .env, secrets, or private API keys to version control.

# ===========================================================================
# 1. Backend API Base URL
# ===========================================================================
# In local development:
#   Leave blank or set to /api. Vite dev proxy (configured in vite.config.js)
#   automatically forwards requests to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
# In production (e.g. deployed on Vercel):
#   Set to your public Django REST API domain (e.g. https://api.keyflow.app/api
#   or https://your-backend.railway.app/api).
VITE_API_URL=

# ===========================================================================
# 2. Clerk Authentication (Unified Identity & Google OAuth)
# ===========================================================================
# Obtain from your Clerk Dashboard -> API Keys -> Publishable Key:
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
#   Use your Clerk Development Instance Publishable Key:
#   VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
#
#   * NOTE ON DEVELOPMENT CONSOLE NOTICE:
#     When loaded with a pk_test_ key, Clerk's JavaScript SDK deliberately emits:
#       "Clerk: Clerk has been loaded with development keys. Development instances
#        have strict usage limits and should not be used when deploying your application to production."
#     This is standard Clerk SDK behavior designed to ensure development keys
#     are never deployed into live production environments.
#
# PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT:
#   In your hosting provider dashboard (e.g. Vercel, Railway, Cloudflare Pages),
#   set VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY to your Clerk Production Instance Publishable Key:
#   VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_...
#
#   When loaded with a pk_live_ key on your custom production domain, the Clerk
#   SDK operates in full production mode and suppresses the development notice.
#
# CRITICAL SECURITY RULE:
#   NEVER set or expose Clerk Secret Keys (sk_test_... or sk_live_...) in frontend
#   environment files. Secret keys belong exclusively on the Django backend.
# ===========================================================================
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...

# Note: Google OAuth is configured directly in Clerk Dashboard (Configure -> SSO Connections -> Google).
# No frontend Google Client ID or GIS script is needed.

# ===========================================================================
# Backend Pairing Reference (Configured in backend/.env)
# ===========================================================================
# The frontend relies on the Django backend for authentication and email delivery.
# Ensure your backend/.env is also configured with:
#   - FRONTEND_URL: Public URL of this frontend (e.g. http://localhost:5173 or https://keyflow.app)
#   - CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY: Matching pk_test_ (in dev) or pk_live_ (in prod)
#   - CLERK_SECRET_KEY: Matching sk_test_ (in dev) or sk_live_ (in prod)
#   - EMAIL_BACKEND / SMTP settings: For real password reset email delivery
